1
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,540
B1.

2
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:13,610
David and Nora are visiting the Natural History Museum.

3
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:20,950
Listen to them talking to the guide and matching the pictures with the correct information.

4
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:25,110
That's a funny bird.

5
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:29,650
I've never seen a bird like that before.

6
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:31,960
That's a dodo.

7
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:35,560
They lived on Earth a long time ago.

8
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:40,430
You mean there aren't any left? That's right.

9
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:43,710
Oh, that's too bad.

10
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:46,950
Look at this! Wow!

11
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:49,380
It's so big!

12
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:52,230
That's a blue whale.

13
00:00:52,230 --> 00:00:57,050
Are there a lot of blue whales? No.

14
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:04,460
There are only about 10,000 to 25,000 blue whales around the world.

15
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:11,280
If we don't stop hunting them, soon there'll be none left. Look!

16
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:13,830
This is a tiger.

17
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:17,720
Yes, it's a South China tiger.

18
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:23,400
There are few left in the world. That's sad.

19
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,850
What about this bird?

20
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:28,760
This is a bald eagle.

21
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:36,440
It was once in danger, but not anymore because people have stopped hunting them.
